WEBVTT

00:00:00.411 --> 00:00:02.994
In this video, you will judge a contest.

00:00:02.994 --> 00:00:10.859
You will open your invitation email, see how your ballot works, and pick or score the homes, including what to do when you know the household.

00:00:11.704 --> 00:00:13.881
This is your invitation email.

00:00:13.881 --> 00:00:18.210
It says which contest it is, who invited you, and how judging works.

00:00:18.210 --> 00:00:20.884
The organizer chooses one of two methods.

00:00:20.884 --> 00:00:26.202
Either you pick a favorite home in each category, or you score every home from one to ten.

00:00:26.202 --> 00:00:28.213
This contest uses scores.

00:00:28.213 --> 00:00:30.717
Everything you need is behind one button.

00:00:30.717 --> 00:00:32.587
Tap Open my judges' ballot.

00:00:35.136 --> 00:00:36.513
This is your ballot.

00:00:36.513 --> 00:00:42.063
It says when voting closes, and how many are done, so you always know how far along you are.

00:00:42.063 --> 00:00:46.832
Your picks or scores stay private, and you can change them until voting closes.

00:00:47.678 --> 00:00:50.737
Before you score, you may want to see the homes in person.

00:00:50.737 --> 00:00:52.008
Tap Visit the homes.

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:59.688
A long list is split into routes of nine stops or fewer, and each one opens in your maps app.

00:00:59.688 --> 00:01:04.028
Each route starts where the last one ended, and you tick off each home as you go.

00:01:04.916 --> 00:01:06.216
Now tap a category.

00:01:07.921 --> 00:01:10.337
Every home is in every category.

00:01:10.337 --> 00:01:17.681
If the organizer chose to pick a favorite, each home has a Pick button, and after you pick, the others say Move my pick.

00:01:17.681 --> 00:01:21.096
In this contest, you score each home once for each award.

00:01:21.967 --> 00:01:25.142
Do you know the household, perhaps a friend or a relative?

00:01:25.142 --> 00:01:26.695
Tap I know this household.

00:01:28.307 --> 00:01:32.038
That home is skipped for you, so your score cannot be questioned later.

00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:35.835
Score each of the other homes from one to ten.

00:01:35.835 --> 00:01:40.061
If your contest uses picks, you would tap Pick on your favorite instead.

00:01:40.061 --> 00:01:45.933
Judge on first impression, creativity, theme, craftsmanship, and variety of lights.

00:01:46.796 --> 00:01:48.560
Tap Ballot to see your progress.

00:01:50.126 --> 00:01:52.709
When you have scored every home, you are done.

00:01:52.709 --> 00:01:55.459
Your scores stay private until the winners are announced.

00:01:56.312 --> 00:01:58.905
Next up: Create a contest with Quick start.
